@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Short Slug Identity
  "Mints 6-character base62 slug identities and maintains the manifest reservation table."

  Provides:
    - domain.SlugLength @source("symbol:SlugLength")
    - domain.ValidateSlug @source("symbol:ValidateSlug")
    - domain.MintSlug @source("symbol:MintSlug")
    - domain.MintSlugWith @source("symbol:MintSlugWith")
    - domain.Manifest.SlugReserved @source("symbol:SlugReserved")
    - domain.Manifest.ReserveSlug @source("symbol:ReserveSlug")
    - domain.Manifest.MintAndReserveSlug @source("symbol:MintAndReserveSlug")

  Consumes:
    - domain.Manifest

  Invariants:
    - Slugs MUST be exactly SlugLength base62 characters
    - Reserved slugs MUST NOT be auto-reused for different content
    - MintAndReserveSlug MUST record the reservation before returning the slug

  Scenario (happy-path): Mint unused slug
    Given a reservation predicate that rejects taken slugs
    When MintSlug runs
    Then it returns a valid 6-character base62 slug not already reserved

  Scenario (happy-path): Reserve on manifest
    Given a fresh slug
    When ReserveSlug runs on a manifest
    Then the slug appears in reserved_slugs exactly once

  Scenario (negative): Invalid slug shape
    Given a slug with wrong length or non-base62 characters
    When ValidateSlug runs
    Then it returns an error

  Scenario (negative): Exhausted mint retries
    Given a reservation predicate that rejects every candidate
    When MintSlug runs
    Then it fails after bounded attempts
